With no request body, req.body is an empty map, so reading a member of it
gives NIL rather than a NIL ACCESS ERROR (Requirement 7.2, 3.8).

### GET with no body
GET /body
=> 200

{"body": {}, "name": null}

### POST with no body
POST /body
=> 200

{"body": {}, "name": null}

### POST with a body, for contrast
POST /body

{"name": "Casper"}
=> 200

{"body": {"name": "Casper"}, "name": "Casper"}
